        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall the root वट meaning विभाजने — it resembles वटि विभाजने from the curadi gana, which gives वण्टयति, so I'm checking whether वट here is meant as an akarant variant of that same root.\n\nSince other curadi roots without ँ seem to be written plain, I'll treat \"वट\" as adanta too, giving वटयति. That means the āśīrliṅ third person plural parasmaipada would be वट्यासुः, with ṇi-lopa before the ārdhadhātuka ending.\n\nI'm scanning through the curadi/bhvadi dhatupatha list looking for \"वट\" among roots like वर, गण, शठ, पट, रह, स्तन, पत, स्वर, रच, कल, मह, सार, स्पृह, भाम, सूच, खेट — trying to pin down its exact gana placement and meaning to settle whether it's adanta or not.\n\nSo taking वट with meaning विभाजने as the akārānta root, the form would be वट्यासुः.\n\n",
